(11)"Association" means the association / association of Ship
Recycling Facility owners who are engaged in ship recycling
and duly approved by the SRB;

(44) “Prescribed” means prescribed by decisions, notifications
or circulations of the Ship Recycling Board made under this
Rule;

(ii) failure to commence the operation of the SRF within 3
(three) years of taking over the lease, except in the case of
sub-rule 4 (i);

(3) authorize a ship recycling facility, approve ship recycling
plan and issue permission for ship recycling in the manner
specified in regulations;

(7) carry out enquiry or inspection in the manner as prescribed
by the guidelines adopted by the relevant MEPC resolution as
applicable and the Rules;

(11) carry out environmental impact assessment at intervals
not exceeding two years in the manner as prescribed by the
Board;

(vii) A declaration by the owner of the SRF that the hazardous
waste of the ship shall be managed in accordance with the
existing Rules;

(viii) a money receipt for depositing the amount determined by
the Government in favour of the Board in respect of the No
Objection Certificate;

(ii) the ship's inventory of hazardous materials (IHM) and
updated by a competent organization as prescribed by the
Board;

(vii) Receipt of fee deposit at the rate of the amount fixed by
the Board per ship weight / LDT in favour of the Board for
recycling or cutting fee;

(3) matters relating to liaison and cooperation with national
and international organizations / organizations in ship
recycling activities;

(i) the discovery and production of books of account and other
documents, at such place and such time as may be specified by
the Secretary, and examining them on oath;

requisitioning any public record or document or a copy of such
record or document, from any office and production of such
documents;

